{
 "schema": "ipr-noise-probe-v001",
 "created_utc": "20261029T201816Z",
 "author": "Claude",
 "question": "The user sees a much better camera denoise when 'automatic white balance' is checked. That option skips IPR's signed development (developedByIpr) and LibRaw's dcraw_process develops instead. Is the gain due to the signed negatives, or to something else?",
 "base": {
  "commit": "75d87010cb4366036623d37b6a6fa21194b93093",
  "camera_denoise": "V1 (dec3c6f)",
  "reference": "docs/validation/raw/loi-force-bruit-v001-20261029T185322Z.json",
  "masks_and_alignment": "those of the reference; windows = 320x320 with most mask pixels (crops kept locally, not committed)"
 },
 "variants": {
  "signed": "engine of 75d8701 unchanged: camera WB, signed development, camera denoise",
  "unsigned": {
   "change": "RawDecoder: the Signed policy never selected (if (false && options.signedDevelopment)), development of LibRaw parity, clamped at 0; camera WB; same denoise",
   "executable_sha256": "6dfaf4d748259a4303855a192d6f00a0e8870edaca880c84a1a762cc913c5e30"
  },
  "autowb": {
   "change": "decodeCr3: options.automaticWhiteBalance forced when IPR_PROBE_AUTOWB is set: LibRaw grey-world WB, dcraw_process, and no normalization manifest (RawNormalization requires the camera WB); same denoise",
   "executable_sha256": "not recorded"
  }
 },
 "metrics": "as the reference, plus dots = share of mask pixels whose 8-bit R-G or B-G departs by more than 12 from its 9x9 median",
 "reading": [
  "signed vs unsigned (camera WB): small difference; unsigned has fewer coloured dots in 7599 shadows at 100/100 (dark dots rg 0.9% -> 0.2%, chroma 1.5 -> 1.0) but lifts the blacks (dark luma 12.6 -> 18.5); 6V1A9539 identical. The negatives are not the main cause.",
  "autowb: the image is darker (7599 mid_flat luma 61.7 -> 46.0, bright 202 -> 181: no normalization manifest) and cooler (grey world on a yellow wall). Its noise is lower from the start (0/0/0 dark luma noise 11.0 -> 8.2) and the denoise acts in the same proportions: the camera denoise still runs (bright_flat luma 7.8 at 100/100, the current denoise A would give 3.5).",
  "the visible gain with automatic WB is therefore mostly a darker, cooler rendering where the same residual noise shows less; it is not a better denoise.",
  "on every path, 100/100 leaves low-frequency colour blotches (teal/magenta, about 10-20 px) in the mid flats of 7599: the next visible target."
 ],
 "scripts_sha256": {
  "signed_probe.py": "a0d68312e4265d1af37a66816d2a3b506fa8376c4e4d56e5d4574de31ddc7be0",
  "strength_law.py": "6a2908cc02c68eef0648855ecacaa702935c61c275c363b4a7303b671a03f914"
 },
 "scripts_source": {
  "signed_probe.py": "\"\"\"Camera denoise on two developments, same masks as the reference. Usage:\npython signed_probe.py EXE REFERENCE.json LABEL OUT_DIR scene...\"\"\"\nimport json, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as np, cv2\nsys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).parent))\nfrom strength_law import BASE, RenderServer, masks, metrics, read8  # noqa: E402\n\nSTATES = (\"0/0/0\", \"70/25/0\", \"100/0/0\", \"0/100/0\", \"100/100/0\")\n\n\ndef window(mask, size=320):\n    \"\"\"Top-left corner of the size x size window with most mask pixels.\"\"\"\n    integral = cv2.integral(mask.astype(np.uint8))\n    sums = integral[size:, size:] - integral[:-size, size:] - integral[size:, :-size] + integral[:-size, :-size]\n    y, x = np.unravel_index(np.argmax(sums), sums.shape)\n    return int(x), int(y)\n\n\ndef dots(im, mask):\n    \"\"\"Share of mask pixels whose 8-bit R-G or B-G departs by more than 12 from a 9x9 median.\"\"\"\n    out = {}\n    for name, c in ((\"rg\", im[..., 0] - im[..., 1]), (\"bg\", im[..., 2] - im[..., 1])):\n        med = cv2.medianBlur(np.clip(c + 128, 0, 255).astype(np.uint8), 9).astype(np.float32) - 128\n        out[name] = round(float((np.abs(c - med)[mask] > 12).mean()), 5)\n    return out\n\n\nexe, ref, label, outdir = Path(sys.argv[1]), json.loads(Path(sys.argv[2]).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")), sys.argv[3], Path(sys.argv[4])\noutdir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nreport = {}\nwith RenderServer(exe, timeout=900) as server:\n    for scene in sys.argv[5:]:\n        s = ref[\"scenes\"][scene]\n        ca = s[\"masks\"][\"common_area\"]\n        (lx, ly), (ix, iy), (w, h) = ca[\"lr_origin_xy\"], ca[\"ipr_origin_xy\"], ca[\"size_wh\"]\n        lr = read8(BASE / \"neutre\" / f\"{scene}.tif\")[ly:ly + h, lx:lx + w]\n        m = masks(lr)\n        wins = {z: window(m[z]) for z in (\"dark\", \"mid_flat\")}\n        raw = next(p for p in BASE.iterdir() if p.stem == scene and p.suffix.upper() in (\".CR3\", \".CR2\"))\n        report[scene] = {\"windows_xy\": wins}\n        for key in STATES:\n            lum, col, _ = map(int, key.split(\"/\"))\n            im = server.render(raw, \"neutral\", 0, camera_denoise={\"luminance\": lum, \"chrominance\": col})[0]\n            im = im[iy:iy + h, ix:ix + w]\n            f = im.astype(np.float32) / 257.0\n            report[scene][key] = {\"metrics\": metrics(f, m), \"dots_dark\": dots(f, m[\"dark\"]) if m[\"dark\"].sum() > 2000 else None,\n                                  \"dots_mid_flat\": dots(f, m[\"mid_flat\"])}\n            for z, (x, y) in wins.items():\n                crop = cv2.cvtColor((im[y:y + 320, x:x + 320] // 257).astype(np.uint8), cv2.COLOR_RGB2BGR)\n                cv2.imwrite(str(outdir / f\"{scene}_{z}_{label}_{key.replace('/', '-')}.png\"), crop)\n            print(scene, key, report[scene][key], flush=True)\n(outdir / f\"{label}.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report, indent=1))\n"
 },
